# machines - Nix distributed build farm configuration
# Format: https://nixos.org/manual/nix/stable/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.html
#
# Each line: [protocol://]user@host system ssh-key max-jobs speed-factor supported-features mandatory-features
# Note: Empty fields use defaults, - means "not specified"

# All 4 cluster nodes are build servers (base x86_64, reverted from v3 on 2026-03-14)

# Zephyr - K8s control plane + node (32 cores, 31GB RAM)
# DISABLED as builder: maxJobs=0 (only 31GB RAM, OOMs building large packages like gamescope)
# Previous: maxJobs=4 (~7.5GB per job, leaves 1GB headroom for system + AI)
ssh-ng://j_kro@zephyr x86_64-linux - 0 1 kvm,big-parallel -

# Nexus - K8s storage worker + NFS (24 cores, 46GB RAM)
# maxJobs=2 (~7GB per job, leaves 4GB headroom for NFS)
ssh-ng://j_kro@nexus x86_64-linux - 6 5 big-parallel -

# Forge - GPU worker (6 cores, 15GB RAM, 2x RTX 4060 + 2x RX 5700 XT)
# CONSERVATIVE maxJobs=1 (only 15GB RAM, GPU workloads need memory)
ssh-ng://j_kro@forge x86_64-linux - 1 2 big-parallel -

# Sentry - Monitoring worker (16 cores, 31GB RAM, RX 5600 XT)
# maxJobs=3 (~15GB per job, leaves headroom for monitoring stack)
ssh-ng://j_kro@sentry x86_64-linux - 2 3 big-parallel -
